<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Currency conversion</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p> A tourist converted £{@init_amnt@} into Kenyan Shillings (KSH) at the rate of {@float(ex_rate)@} KSH to £\(1\).</p>

<p> He spent {@spent@} KSH</p>
<p>He then converted the rest back into pounds at the same exchange rate.</p>
<p>How many pounds did he have left?</p>
<p>Give your answer to \(2\) decimal places.</p>
<p>Amount of pounds left \(=\) £[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]][[feedback:prt1]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked Solution</h3>
<p></p>
<p>Convert pounds to Kenyan shillings:</p>
<p>\({{@init_amnt@}} \times {@float(ex_rate)@} ={@init_amnt_ksh@}\)</p>
<p>Subtract the money spent:</P>
<p>\({@init_amnt_ksh@}-{@spent@} ={@bal_ksh@}\)</p>
<p>Convert back to pounds:</p>
<p>\({@bal_ksh@} \div {@float(ex_rate)@} = {@dispdp(bal_pounds,2)@}\)</p>
<p>Final answer is £\({@dispdp(bal_pounds,2)@}\)</p>
<p><br></p>
<p>A quick way to do this is to convert the shillings spent into pounds:</p>
<p>\({@spent@}\div{@float(ex_rate)@}={@spent_pounds@}\)</p>
<p>Subtract this from the orginal:</p>
<p>\({@init_amnt@}-{@spent_pounds@}=£{@dispdp(bal_pounds,2)@}\)</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>3</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <idnumber/>
    <stackversion>
      <text>2023060500</text>
    </stackversion>
    <questionvariables>
      <text>init_amnt:10*(rand(50)+50);

ex_rate:rand_with_prohib(1351,1619,[1360,1370,1380,1390,1400,1410,1420,1430,1440,1450,1460,1470,1480,1490,1500,1510,1520,1530,1540,1550,1560,1570,1580,1590,1600,1610])/10;

spent:rand([6,8,9])*(rand(60)+500);

/*model solution*/
init_amnt_ksh:init_amnt*ex_rate;
bal_ksh:init_amnt_ksh-spent;
bal_pounds:bal_ksh/ex_rate;

bal_2_dp:decimalplaces(bal_pounds,2);

/*alternative solution*/
spent_pounds:decimalplaces(spent/ex_rate,2);</text>
    </questionvariables>
